WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.835
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:06.105 --> 00:07.545
I'll be waiting for good news!

3
00:07.625 --> 00:09.265
Make sure you bring back that million.

4
00:11.665 --> 00:12.945
Good night.

5
00:15.545 --> 00:19.465
Everyone must live and play the game here for seven days.

6
00:19.545 --> 00:21.345
Whoever is the last one standing

7
00:21.425 --> 00:23.665
will take home a prize of ten million baht.

8
00:23.745 --> 00:24.705
Hey.

9
00:24.785 --> 00:25.905
It's because of him, isn't it?

10
00:25.985 --> 00:27.385
The one named Pee.

11
00:27.465 --> 00:29.505
I can't live without him.

12
00:29.585 --> 00:31.705
But you still have me.

13
00:31.785 --> 00:33.985
I told you not to trust anyone in this game.

14
01:01.385 --> 01:02.625
Fuck!

15
01:04.105 --> 01:05.905
They got rid of the bodies so fast.

16
01:05.985 --> 01:08.705
It's like a game. When someone dies, they just disappear.

17
01:08.785 --> 01:10.665
Are you still going to defend them

18
01:10.745 --> 01:12.625
and say it's just a reality show?

19
01:15.465 --> 01:17.225
Are we gonna make it out of here alive?

20
01:23.185 --> 01:25.785
Don't forget, I'm the bodyguard.

21
01:25.865 --> 01:28.825
Of course I can keep you safe.

22
01:31.625 --> 01:34.625
But you're not mad I chose to save Wut last round, right?

23
01:36.625 --> 01:37.745
I understand.

24
01:38.705 --> 01:40.185
If you keep choosing me,

25
01:40.985 --> 01:43.225
everyone will figure out you're the bodyguard.

26
01:47.025 --> 01:48.185
You've got a point.

27
01:51.105 --> 01:53.225
We're practically inseparable.

28
01:53.305 --> 01:54.825
It wouldn't be hard to guess.

29
02:00.185 --> 02:01.825
But you need to look after yourself too.

30
02:01.905 --> 02:03.705
Don't just worry about me.

31
02:03.785 --> 02:06.025
What? Who's worried about you?

32
02:07.105 --> 02:08.584
I'm the bodyguard.

33
02:08.665 --> 02:10.705
As long as I protect myself every round,

34
02:10.785 --> 02:12.105
I'll survive.

35
02:13.185 --> 02:15.185
Yeah, whatever.

36
02:16.745 --> 02:18.625
And if those damn wolves come after me,

37
02:19.185 --> 02:20.905
I'll fight back for sure.

38
02:23.305 --> 02:25.665
But I'd rather escape from here.

39
02:25.745 --> 02:27.025
Let's not risk it.

40
02:27.705 --> 02:28.985
How are you gonna escape?

41
02:29.065 --> 02:31.465
Those damn rabbits are all over the house.

42
02:31.545 --> 02:33.825
I've seen them. They're all good shots.

43
02:37.305 --> 02:39.625
But I think they must have some weakness.

44
02:41.305 --> 02:44.065
For now, you and I have to play along.

45
02:44.145 --> 02:45.705
Don't let them catch on.

46
02:50.505 --> 02:52.625
Ten million isn't fucking worth it.

47
02:59.105 --> 03:01.305
Oh, right. While you were hiding,

48
03:01.385 --> 03:03.025
did you see the wolf's face?

49
03:03.585 --> 03:04.905
I didn't see his face.

50
03:05.985 --> 03:07.385
I only saw his legs.

51
03:11.585 --> 03:13.905
But I'm sure he's a man.

52
03:21.985 --> 03:23.505
We'd better hide inside for now.

53
03:32.305 --> 03:33.145
Come on.

54
06:00.825 --> 06:02.345
You're up early.

55
06:02.425 --> 06:04.225
I thought you said you were a night owl.

56
06:06.265 --> 06:07.465
What about you?

57
06:07.545 --> 06:10.825
Don't writers usually wake up in the afternoon?

58
06:12.105 --> 06:13.345
I'm the exception.

59
06:16.905 --> 06:18.625
Do you wake up this early every day?

60
06:20.425 --> 06:23.145
Not really. I can't sleep.

61
06:25.825 --> 06:27.025
How many days?

62
06:30.225 --> 06:33.025
I mean, how many days have you been unable to sleep?

63
06:36.225 --> 06:37.745
I don't know.

64
06:37.825 --> 06:39.025
I haven't been counting.

65
06:40.025 --> 06:42.945
I take medication, but it doesn't seem to work.

66
06:44.065 --> 06:46.345
I have to wait until sunrise

67
06:47.905 --> 06:50.825
before I can feel at ease and get some sleep.

68
06:54.145 --> 06:57.145
Or maybe… you're a vampire.

69
06:58.425 --> 07:00.345
Awake at night, asleep during the day.

70
07:00.425 --> 07:01.745
Allergic to sunlight and all that.

71
07:01.825 --> 07:03.225
Let me see your fangs.

72
07:03.905 --> 07:06.545
You've got a wilder imagination than a novelist like me.

73
07:07.225 --> 07:08.665
Well, I spend so much time with you.

74
07:08.745 --> 07:10.025
I have to adapt a little.

75
07:18.105 --> 07:19.825
Whenever you're ready,

76
07:19.905 --> 07:21.305
you can tell me about it.

77
08:27.265 --> 08:28.825
LAY LAMOE BEACH BAR

78
08:28.905 --> 08:30.265
I'm hungry.

79
08:31.025 --> 08:32.025
What should we eat?

80
08:32.705 --> 08:34.904
-Let's see what they have inside. -Okay.

81
08:40.105 --> 08:42.745
Perfect timing, Talay, Sun.

82
08:42.825 --> 08:45.785
I have to go to Bangkok for a couple of days.

83
08:45.865 --> 08:49.825
If… you want anything to eat or drink, it's all in the fridge.

84
08:49.905 --> 08:52.625
-Take care of the place. Bye! -Sure.

85
08:53.705 --> 08:56.425
-Shall we check the kitchen? -Sure, let's go.

86
09:39.185 --> 09:40.905
Between the rice porridge and me,

87
09:41.745 --> 09:42.905
which tastes better?

88
09:46.105 --> 09:47.825
The rice porridge, obviously.

89
09:47.905 --> 09:49.105
This early in the morning,

90
09:49.185 --> 09:52.025
something hot goes down smoothly and refreshes me.

91
09:52.105 --> 09:53.945
But someone like you,

92
09:54.025 --> 09:56.345
I'd need lots of water to wash you down.

93
09:56.425 --> 09:57.745
You're too dry.

94
10:01.025 --> 10:02.745
You weren't like this last night.

95
10:03.625 --> 10:05.705
I thought I was pretty hot.

96
10:12.305 --> 10:13.825
But that person's name is Pee, right?

97
10:17.225 --> 10:19.145
You even searched for news about him?

98
10:21.545 --> 10:22.625
Is he your ex?

99
10:26.225 --> 10:27.625
He used to be my assistant.

100
10:31.505 --> 10:33.225
Judging by your reaction,

101
10:34.505 --> 10:36.345
he wasn't just an assistant.

102
10:41.545 --> 10:44.225
To me, that's true.

103
10:44.305 --> 10:45.745
He was more than an assistant.

104
10:46.705 --> 10:50.265
But to him, I never meant anything.

105
10:51.425 --> 10:53.145
You got your heart broken,

106
10:53.225 --> 10:55.105
so you can't write romance novels anymore?

107
10:56.625 --> 10:58.185
That's not like you at all.

108
10:58.265 --> 11:00.425
Just because one person let you down

109
11:00.505 --> 11:03.265
doesn't mean your whole world has to fall apart.

110
11:06.225 --> 11:07.425
What about you?

111
11:07.505 --> 11:10.065
You keep playing hard to get, refusing my offer.

112
11:10.145 --> 11:12.465
And I can see you drawing boundaries.

113
11:12.545 --> 11:14.225
You've built walls.

114
11:14.305 --> 11:16.665
You refuse to date anyone.

115
11:17.305 --> 11:20.305
Are you saying you've never been hurt?

116
11:20.385 --> 11:23.425
Why? Come on, tell me.

117
11:23.505 --> 11:25.545
Who broke your heart so badly

118
11:26.105 --> 11:28.265
that you don't believe in love anymore?

119
11:29.505 --> 11:30.865
You don't need to know.

120
11:32.425 --> 11:34.545
But things are good between us like this.

121
11:35.105 --> 11:37.625
No labels. No commitments.

122
11:38.825 --> 11:41.105
And we can't hurt each other

123
11:42.025 --> 11:43.505
because we're nothing to each other.

124
11:44.145 --> 11:46.865
What do you think? Sounds fair, doesn't it?

125
11:48.905 --> 11:51.745
So… we only share the good times,

126
11:51.825 --> 11:53.025
not the bad? Is that it?

127
12:04.905 --> 12:07.665
And when you told me last night

128
12:07.745 --> 12:09.025
that I still had you…

129
12:11.825 --> 12:14.705
was that part of pretending we were dating too?

130
12:19.705 --> 12:20.705
Yes.

131
12:21.425 --> 12:22.505
I guess it was.

132
12:51.905 --> 12:53.705
The first night is over.

133
12:54.345 --> 12:57.425
All remaining players, please proceed to the dining room.

134
13:03.705 --> 13:04.745
Yoyeh.

135
13:05.545 --> 13:06.545
Yoyeh.

136
13:07.305 --> 13:08.305
Wake up.

137
13:16.905 --> 13:17.905
Is it over?

138
13:56.145 --> 13:57.545
-I'm starving. -Me too.

139
13:57.625 --> 13:59.145
-Seriously. -What is there to eat?

140
13:59.225 --> 14:00.225
Here.

141
14:14.665 --> 14:15.905
Here it is.

142
14:33.825 --> 14:35.545
How can anyone eat after seeing that?

143
14:45.425 --> 14:47.945
Hey. Don't worry.

144
14:48.025 --> 14:49.785
Neither of us is a wolf.

145
14:50.425 --> 14:52.505
We almost got killed yesterday.

146
14:53.505 --> 14:54.825
Luckily, we survived.

147
14:55.905 --> 14:56.905
Really?

148
14:57.505 --> 15:00.625
Then… why are you two always together?

149
15:01.625 --> 15:02.825
Are you two dating?

150
15:03.505 --> 15:04.625
-No. -No.

151
15:08.345 --> 15:09.825
We're just old friends.

152
15:11.305 --> 15:12.825
You're friends.

153
15:12.905 --> 15:17.105
But… you and that guy named Cha are friends too, right?

154
15:19.545 --> 15:21.385
That asshole? Don't count him as my friend.

155
15:32.225 --> 15:35.225
I think… we should team up.

156
15:36.185 --> 15:37.545
Because at least,

157
15:37.625 --> 15:40.705
if tonight we vote out one wolf,

158
15:41.745 --> 15:43.625
there'll only be one wolf left.

159
15:44.545 --> 15:47.625
That means we can survive another night.

160
15:48.225 --> 15:49.345
Right.

161
15:49.425 --> 15:52.865
One wolf left against six villagers.

162
15:52.945 --> 15:54.345
We can easily take him down together.

163
15:57.545 --> 15:59.345
You two saw the wolf last night?

164
15:59.425 --> 16:00.705
Tell me about it.

165
16:04.945 --> 16:06.745
I didn't actually see his face.

166
16:07.425 --> 16:08.945
We were hiding.

167
16:09.025 --> 16:11.545
But I'm sure he's a man.

168
16:12.345 --> 16:13.425
I agree.

169
16:13.945 --> 16:15.745
Last night,

170
16:15.825 --> 16:18.025
I saw the wolf's shadow while he was hunting.

171
16:18.105 --> 16:19.465
He was really tall.

172
16:19.545 --> 16:22.585
About 180 centimeters.

173
16:22.665 --> 16:25.225
I also think he's definitely a man.

174
16:26.905 --> 16:28.585
Then that leaves

175
16:28.665 --> 16:29.945
Au,

176
16:31.385 --> 16:32.545
Nack,

177
16:33.625 --> 16:34.745
and Cha.

178
16:38.505 --> 16:40.625
You can't say there are only three suspects.

179
16:41.545 --> 16:42.905
There have to be five.

180
16:44.545 --> 16:46.665
Au, Nack,

181
16:46.745 --> 16:49.865
Cha, and you two.

182
16:49.945 --> 16:51.145
Hey!

183
16:51.225 --> 16:53.425
Actually, Wut too. That makes six.

184
16:54.425 --> 16:55.545
I'm not a wolf.

185
16:57.425 --> 16:58.745
Who knows?

186
16:58.825 --> 17:02.825
Maybe you two are lying.

187
17:04.305 --> 17:06.464
I'm not going to throw my life away here.

188
17:15.224 --> 17:17.025
Good morning. It's day two.

189
17:18.345 --> 17:21.825
There are now eight players remaining.

190
17:22.865 --> 17:25.464
Please enjoy the food

191
17:25.545 --> 17:27.224
and comfortable beds we've provided.

192
17:27.905 --> 17:29.265
I ate better than this at the club.

193
17:30.425 --> 17:31.825
At 3 p.m. today,

194
17:31.905 --> 17:33.705
we'll play Capture the Flag.

195
17:34.465 --> 17:35.625
Capture the Flag?

196
17:36.625 --> 17:38.545
-What's that? -We'll divide you into two teams,

197
17:38.625 --> 17:39.665
four players each.

198
17:39.745 --> 17:43.705
Each team must protect its own flag.

199
17:43.785 --> 17:46.025
One player will carry the flag,

200
17:46.105 --> 17:47.785
while the other three will devise a strategy

201
17:47.865 --> 17:50.145
to capture the opposing team's flag.

202
17:51.225 --> 17:52.665
The rule is,

203
17:52.745 --> 17:55.745
the opposing team cannot attack you

204
17:55.825 --> 17:57.545
unless you enter their territory.

205
17:58.305 --> 18:01.265
Most importantly, each player

206
18:01.345 --> 18:04.225
will wear a team-colored armband.

207
18:04.305 --> 18:06.065
If any player

208
18:06.145 --> 18:08.025
loses their armband to the opposing team,

209
18:08.625 --> 18:10.025
they're out.

210
18:10.745 --> 18:12.945
The staff have also drawn lots

211
18:13.025 --> 18:14.425
to assign you to teams.

212
18:14.865 --> 18:16.905
Team A will be on the left.

213
18:16.985 --> 18:19.665
The members are Natty,

214
18:20.305 --> 18:21.545
Tangmo,

215
18:22.625 --> 18:25.265
Wut, and Cha.

216
18:36.105 --> 18:37.785
Team B will be on the right.

217
18:39.185 --> 18:41.745
The members are May,

218
18:44.425 --> 18:45.625
Nack,

219
18:47.745 --> 18:50.745
Au, and Yoyeh.

220
18:57.945 --> 18:59.905
Hey, what kind of team selection is this?

221
18:59.985 --> 19:02.465
You're putting me on the same team as Cha?

222
19:02.545 --> 19:04.585
-Because you're a pro. -Pro, my ass!

223
19:04.665 --> 19:06.025
Can you two stop fighting already?

224
19:06.105 --> 19:08.705
The staff's decision is final.

225
19:10.425 --> 19:11.865
Good luck, everyone.

226
19:14.825 --> 19:16.425
See you at 3 p.m.

227
19:17.545 --> 19:18.945
You damn butler!

228
19:19.025 --> 19:21.785
Hey, butler! I'm not staying on this team!

229
19:22.465 --> 19:25.345
-Hey, hey! -Calm down, Tangmo. Just calm down.

230
19:26.025 --> 19:27.265
Listen to me first.

231
19:27.865 --> 19:29.305
This is actually better.

232
19:30.105 --> 19:32.185
We can split up and find out who's a wolf.

233
20:23.545 --> 20:24.945
The rule is,

234
20:25.025 --> 20:28.665
each team must protect its own flag.

235
20:28.745 --> 20:29.745
Most importantly,

236
20:29.825 --> 20:33.385
if any player loses their armband to the opposing team,

237
20:33.465 --> 20:35.545
they're out.

238
20:35.625 --> 20:36.745
Good luck, everyone.

239
20:37.945 --> 20:39.025
You.

240
20:39.105 --> 20:40.425
Stay here and guard the flag with May.

241
20:40.505 --> 20:42.305
You'll only slow me down if you come.

242
20:42.905 --> 20:44.225
Let's all go together.

243
20:44.305 --> 20:47.305
They won't expect us to leave the flag unguarded.

244
20:48.625 --> 20:49.825
Then why don't we split up?

245
20:49.905 --> 20:51.625
We can take them down together.

246
20:52.905 --> 20:55.425
No. Someone has to guard the flag.

247
21:03.025 --> 21:04.225
You stay here.

248
21:04.305 --> 21:06.425
Wut, come with me.

249
21:06.505 --> 21:08.705
-Okay. -I want to come too.

250
21:09.625 --> 21:12.145
I may be small, but I'm good at dodging.

251
21:13.105 --> 21:14.585
You two can be the decoys,

252
21:15.105 --> 21:16.305
and I'll grab the flag.

253
21:17.505 --> 21:19.545
Nobody needs to guard the flag.

254
21:20.105 --> 21:21.785
Let's all go together.

255
21:22.425 --> 21:24.145
I agree.

256
21:24.225 --> 21:26.665
I think… they'll be surprised.

257
21:27.705 --> 21:29.345
Forget surprising them.

258
21:29.425 --> 21:30.865
They're already gone.

259
21:36.025 --> 21:37.505
Could they be using the same plan?

260
21:43.905 --> 21:45.265
If you want to win this game,

261
21:45.785 --> 21:47.505
we all have to work together.

262
21:52.945 --> 21:54.825
Let's go.

263
22:06.785 --> 22:08.025
Everyone, split up.

264
22:08.105 --> 22:09.185
I'll check downstairs.

265
22:24.025 --> 22:25.585
What kind of plan is this?

266
22:28.305 --> 22:30.065
A plan to mess up your face.

267
22:52.945 --> 22:54.305
Let me go!

268
23:11.545 --> 23:13.065
Go cut them off over there.

269
23:16.425 --> 23:18.945
Player Au, out.

270
23:44.145 --> 23:45.745
Hey, stop!

271
23:45.825 --> 23:47.825
This is too easy.

272
23:47.905 --> 23:50.265
-Hey, you! -And you came alone.

273
23:50.345 --> 23:51.465
Where are you going?

274
23:51.545 --> 23:52.865
Calm down, okay?

275
23:52.945 --> 23:54.025
Please let me go.

276
23:55.505 --> 23:56.505
Don't come any closer.

277
24:00.465 --> 24:01.865
What the fuck?!

278
24:01.945 --> 24:02.985
Fuck! Let me go!

279
24:04.065 --> 24:05.065
Oh, come on!

280
24:05.145 --> 24:07.425
-Aw, how pathetic. -Hey, let me go!

281
24:07.505 --> 24:09.545
-Hey, hey! -What was that?

282
24:09.625 --> 24:11.505
-Too easy, huh? -You asshole!

283
24:13.625 --> 24:15.185
Piece of cake!

284
24:15.705 --> 24:17.185
Fuck you! I'll get you back!

285
24:17.825 --> 24:20.225
-Great plan! -Player Wut, out.

286
25:10.625 --> 25:12.065
What the fuck are you doing?

287
25:12.145 --> 25:13.185
I told you.

288
25:13.265 --> 25:14.945
I'll win my own way.

289
25:15.025 --> 25:16.465
Motherfucker!

290
25:47.225 --> 25:48.225
Tangmo.

291
25:50.105 --> 25:51.265
Come play with me first.

292
26:00.225 --> 26:02.025
I give up! I give up!

293
26:16.825 --> 26:18.785
Player Nack, out.

294
27:11.825 --> 27:13.265
Capture the Flag is over.

295
27:14.145 --> 27:15.745
The red team wins.

296
28:11.425 --> 28:13.225
Congratulations, everyone.

297
28:14.625 --> 28:18.185
Now you must choose between 100,000 each in prize money

298
28:19.225 --> 28:21.185
or a clue as to who the wolves are.

299
28:21.265 --> 28:22.905
I'll take the clue.

300
28:24.065 --> 28:25.225
Let's take the money first.

301
28:26.225 --> 28:27.425
Who knows if the clue will actually help us?

302
28:29.265 --> 28:31.145
I'd take the money too.

303
28:31.225 --> 28:33.065
That much money could keep me going.

304
28:33.145 --> 28:34.505
Why?

305
28:35.105 --> 28:36.785
Afraid they'll find out you're a wolf?

306
28:38.025 --> 28:39.025
That has nothing to do with it.

307
28:50.305 --> 28:52.665
I think… you should choose.

308
28:56.065 --> 28:57.545
I'll take the clue.

309
28:59.865 --> 29:00.945
Okay.

310
29:02.625 --> 29:03.625
Scholarship student.

311
29:08.705 --> 29:09.705
Scholarship student?

312
29:14.065 --> 29:15.225
How the fuck would anyone know?

313
29:36.425 --> 29:37.625
You fucker!

314
29:37.705 --> 29:41.385
I know you colluded with Tangmo.

315
29:41.465 --> 29:43.185
What the fuck are you talking about?

316
29:43.265 --> 29:46.345
You worked together to help their team win.

317
29:47.145 --> 29:49.345
If you make me lose again,

318
29:49.425 --> 29:51.225
you'd better be ready.

319
29:53.505 --> 29:54.785
What are you going to do to him?

320
29:55.385 --> 29:56.745
What are you going to do to him?

321
29:57.545 --> 29:59.665
You two, watch your backs.

322
29:59.745 --> 30:01.705
-Want some, motherfucker? -Tangmo! Stop!

323
30:01.785 --> 30:03.145
Tangmo! Stop!

324
30:04.505 --> 30:05.825
Hey, calm down.

325
30:09.825 --> 30:11.225
Tangmo.

326
30:11.305 --> 30:13.425
Look at me. Calm down.

327
30:23.105 --> 30:24.225
Forget it.

328
30:32.585 --> 30:35.745
Pee's new romance novel explores understanding

329
30:35.825 --> 30:38.065
and healing through simple

330
30:38.145 --> 30:40.545
yet profound conversations between two people with different worldviews.

331
30:40.625 --> 30:42.065
One is sunshine,

332
30:42.145 --> 30:43.585
while the other is the dark side of the moon.

333
30:45.145 --> 30:46.745
You're such a boomer.

334
30:46.825 --> 30:48.505
Having AI read it aloud?

335
30:49.145 --> 30:51.345
Especially with this plot,

336
30:51.425 --> 30:52.545
it sounds so…

337
30:52.625 --> 30:53.825
What's the word?

338
30:53.905 --> 30:55.025
Surreal.

339
30:56.905 --> 30:58.545
The world keeps turning.

340
30:58.625 --> 31:00.345
We just adapt.

341
31:00.425 --> 31:01.745
I'm a slow reader.

342
31:01.825 --> 31:03.625
If there's a tool available, I'll use it.

343
31:04.745 --> 31:05.785
Soon enough,

344
31:05.865 --> 31:08.145
AI will probably take my job.

345
31:09.945 --> 31:12.345
Maybe I should retire now.

346
31:12.425 --> 31:14.225
Then I won't have to rack my brain for ideas.

347
31:15.545 --> 31:18.865
Art, in the end, has to come from humans.

348
31:18.945 --> 31:20.745
AI is just a tool.

349
31:21.545 --> 31:23.305
Actually, I think you write well.

350
31:24.265 --> 31:25.545
Why are you so insecure?

351
31:26.225 --> 31:27.185
What?

352
31:27.265 --> 31:29.345
Didn't you say you were a slow reader?

353
31:29.425 --> 31:31.425
Are you just flattering me?

354
31:32.905 --> 31:35.905
Reading slowly doesn't mean I can't read.

355
31:36.745 --> 31:38.385
I've been reading your work.

356
31:39.225 --> 31:40.785
Your writing is really sharp.

357
31:40.865 --> 31:44.185
Like when Thanwa tells Kim,

358
31:44.825 --> 31:47.025
"Some people taught me to hold on."

359
31:47.545 --> 31:49.945
"Others taught me to let go."

360
31:50.625 --> 31:52.345
"But you're the only one

361
31:52.425 --> 31:54.825
who taught me both at once."

362
31:55.905 --> 31:57.065
That's so damn touching.

363
31:57.145 --> 31:58.145
It's so damn profound.

364
31:59.745 --> 32:04.105
Well, maybe because back then, Pee helped me write it.

365
32:06.305 --> 32:08.025
But you're the main writer.

366
32:08.745 --> 32:10.145
Have some confidence in yourself.

367
32:10.225 --> 32:12.425
You're more talented than you think.

368
32:19.425 --> 32:21.025
I've decided to accept your offer.

369
32:24.505 --> 32:26.665
Huh? What did you say?

370
32:27.905 --> 32:29.305
Are you deaf?

371
32:30.345 --> 32:33.425
If you want me to be the model for a character in your novel,

372
32:34.025 --> 32:34.945
I'll take the job.

373
32:36.345 --> 32:38.505
Are you trying to trick me again?

374
32:39.025 --> 32:40.705
I'm not lying to you.

375
32:41.305 --> 32:43.305
So when you decide to say yes,

376
32:43.385 --> 32:44.985
it's really that simple?

377
32:45.745 --> 32:49.145
If you're looking for someone to make your novel perfect,

378
32:49.225 --> 32:52.945
maybe that someone is me. Let me assure you,

379
32:53.025 --> 32:54.945
I can definitely do better than Pee.

380
32:56.225 --> 32:58.145
Yes! This calls for a celebration!

381
32:58.225 --> 32:59.585
My treat.

382
32:59.665 --> 33:00.785
Hey, wait.

383
33:00.865 --> 33:02.585
I have to drive back to Bangkok.

384
33:02.665 --> 33:03.665
Who cares?

385
33:03.745 --> 33:05.265
If you get drunk, stay another night.

386
33:05.345 --> 33:07.585
Come on. It's on me. Let's go.

387
33:09.505 --> 33:10.705
Calm down.

388
33:10.785 --> 33:12.465
The booze isn't going anywhere.

389
33:17.825 --> 33:18.905
Easy.

390
33:19.945 --> 33:21.825
You played rougher than this in hockey.

391
33:23.225 --> 33:24.905
Here, hold it.

392
33:31.545 --> 33:33.345
What did Au just say to you?

393
33:34.745 --> 33:35.945
He was just making threats.

394
33:36.505 --> 33:37.625
That's just his style.

395
33:40.425 --> 33:42.625
I can't protect you all the time.

396
33:43.225 --> 33:45.345
You need to get stronger.

397
33:45.425 --> 33:47.065
Don't let anyone hurt you.

398
33:48.105 --> 33:49.465
Why?

399
33:49.545 --> 33:51.025
Are you going to run away?

400
33:52.705 --> 33:55.025
If we can't escape, we have to win the game, right?

401
33:56.625 --> 33:58.545
And there can only be one winner.

402
34:00.825 --> 34:01.825
Okay.

403
34:03.505 --> 34:04.625
What about the clue?

404
34:05.905 --> 34:07.625
Why should I tell you?

405
34:07.705 --> 34:09.225
I'm the one who won.

406
34:09.865 --> 34:11.385
For patching you up.

407
34:14.105 --> 34:15.665
Don't you want to get out of here soon?

408
34:17.065 --> 34:18.824
Two heads are better than one.

409
34:21.225 --> 34:23.025
The damn clue says "scholarship student."

410
34:26.025 --> 34:27.425
But from what I've figured out,

411
34:28.545 --> 34:30.145
I think we can rule out the women.

412
34:31.545 --> 34:32.744
Scholarship student…

413
34:34.425 --> 34:36.905
Nack's that old. He's been out of high school for ages.

414
34:39.025 --> 34:41.065
As for Au and Wut,

415
34:41.145 --> 34:42.545
I don't think it's them.

416
34:45.025 --> 34:46.945
Then I think it's Cha.

417
34:47.025 --> 34:49.665
He had an athletic scholarship in college.

418
34:51.105 --> 34:53.665
And when the butler asked if we wanted money or a clue,

419
34:53.744 --> 34:56.225
he immediately said he wanted the money.

420
34:57.465 --> 34:59.905
I bet he doesn't want anyone to know he's a wolf.

421
35:01.905 --> 35:03.025
That's possible.

422
35:05.545 --> 35:07.345
Then let's vote for Cha tonight.

423
35:08.905 --> 35:09.905
He's the most likely suspect.

424
35:13.145 --> 35:14.825
If you see him die right in front of you,

425
35:15.825 --> 35:17.105
won't you feel anything?

426
35:20.145 --> 35:21.625
He used to be your friend.

427
35:24.025 --> 35:25.025
Friend?

428
35:27.025 --> 35:30.305
I used to think we were the best hockey duo.

429
35:30.825 --> 35:32.905
Whenever we competed, we never lost.

430
35:34.305 --> 35:36.825
But out of nowhere, he blamed my father

431
35:36.905 --> 35:38.505
for not making the national team.

432
35:39.505 --> 35:41.625
So he quit and joined the opposing team

433
35:42.225 --> 35:43.825
to compete against me.

434
35:46.025 --> 35:47.545
What would you do?

435
35:50.105 --> 35:51.545
He was probably angry back then.

436
36:00.425 --> 36:03.345
Everyone I trusted fucking lied to me and betrayed me.

437
36:05.825 --> 36:07.225
Whether it was Cha,

438
36:09.305 --> 36:10.345
my father,

439
36:12.265 --> 36:13.505
or even you.

440
36:36.505 --> 36:38.545
Cha! That's dangerous!

441
36:41.625 --> 36:42.945
You made the national team.

442
36:44.825 --> 36:46.625
Where did you hear that?

443
36:46.705 --> 36:48.025
They haven't announced it yet.

444
36:48.105 --> 36:50.945
Don't worry about how I found out.

445
36:51.025 --> 36:52.305
Just answer me.

446
36:52.385 --> 36:54.225
How much did your father pay

447
36:55.105 --> 36:56.825
to get your name on the list?

448
36:56.905 --> 36:58.865
What the fuck are you talking about?

449
36:58.945 --> 37:00.825
How many times have we competed together?

450
37:00.905 --> 37:02.865
We always won championships together.

451
37:02.945 --> 37:05.105
Are you saying those titles were fake?

452
37:05.185 --> 37:07.145
You're so naive.

453
37:07.225 --> 37:08.825
What the fuck?

454
37:08.905 --> 37:10.545
You might think you're good,

455
37:11.065 --> 37:14.345
but don't you know that the many tournaments you won so easily

456
37:15.345 --> 37:17.505
were because your father lobbied your opponents?

457
37:18.345 --> 37:19.625
Your father probably couldn't stand

458
37:20.945 --> 37:23.865
seeing his only son lose.

459
37:23.945 --> 37:25.345
Fine.

460
37:27.225 --> 37:29.985
I'll show you I can do it on my own.

461
37:30.065 --> 37:32.225
I'll withdraw from the national team this time.

462
37:32.905 --> 37:35.465
Then you and I can win this tournament together.

463
37:35.545 --> 37:38.345
I believe we'll both make the national team.

464
37:39.025 --> 37:40.545
That day will never come.

465
37:41.345 --> 37:42.585
I'm transferring to another team.

466
37:44.145 --> 37:46.025
I don't want to live in your shadow anymore.

467
37:50.345 --> 37:51.545
Oh.

468
37:52.825 --> 37:54.425
And here's a friendly warning.

469
37:56.545 --> 37:58.025
It's not just the hockey team

470
37:58.625 --> 38:00.025
your father's been interfering with.

471
38:06.105 --> 38:07.745
My father hired you, didn't he?

472
38:09.825 --> 38:11.305
My father hired you

473
38:11.385 --> 38:13.425
to be my boyfriend, didn't he?

474
38:14.905 --> 38:15.985
Answer me!

475
38:16.905 --> 38:18.505
At first, yes.

476
38:19.905 --> 38:22.905
But my feelings for you… I really do love you.

477
38:26.545 --> 38:28.505
You say you love me…

478
38:31.105 --> 38:32.945
but you took a job from my father.

479
38:36.345 --> 38:38.625
Can you tell me the truth

480
38:39.945 --> 38:41.305
for once?

481
39:15.025 --> 39:16.385
I'm sorry.

482
39:33.345 --> 39:34.945
When did you hire him, huh?

483
39:36.305 --> 39:37.625
Just as you found out.

484
39:40.905 --> 39:42.505
How much did he pay you?

485
39:44.865 --> 39:46.905
How much did he pay you?

486
39:52.225 --> 39:53.265
Why did you do it?

487
39:53.945 --> 39:55.345
Why did you deceive me?

488
39:55.425 --> 39:58.225
Because I wanted you to take over TriCorp.

489
40:01.425 --> 40:02.425
TriCorp?

490
40:03.305 --> 40:05.385
Is TriCorp more important than my life?

491
40:05.465 --> 40:07.385
Do you still see me as your son?

492
40:07.465 --> 40:09.465
You all conspired to deceive me.

493
40:09.545 --> 40:10.985
Was it fun?

494
40:11.065 --> 40:12.705
You enjoyed it, didn't you?

495
40:13.945 --> 40:16.865
Isn't TriCorp the reason you have everything you need?

496
40:25.545 --> 40:27.825
From now on, don't call me your son.

497
40:28.825 --> 40:30.465
And stay out of my life.

498
40:32.105 --> 40:33.305
Let me go.

499
40:40.145 --> 40:41.585
Tangmo…

500
41:01.825 --> 41:04.265
Everyone expresses love differently.

501
41:14.345 --> 41:16.305
Don't you want to reconcile with Cha?

502
41:17.825 --> 41:20.305
I can't change what's already happened.

503
41:21.545 --> 41:23.145
What about you and me?

504
41:33.745 --> 41:35.105
Just focus on surviving.

505
41:35.825 --> 41:37.225
We'll talk about the rest later.

506
41:53.625 --> 41:55.225
Did you need something from me?

507
41:56.305 --> 41:58.265
Tangmo is at the Crow Club.

508
41:59.105 --> 42:01.265
I want you to bring Tangmo home.

509
42:06.705 --> 42:07.785
I'm sorry.

510
42:08.705 --> 42:09.985
I can't do that for you.

511
42:10.945 --> 42:13.585
You'll have to handle this yourself.

512
42:23.025 --> 42:23.905
Scholarship student.

513
42:24.825 --> 42:28.025
-Who's a scholarship student? -Well, it's not me.

514
42:28.665 --> 42:30.345
I heard

515
42:30.425 --> 42:32.945
-the wolf's a scholarship student? -The clue's useless.

516
42:35.945 --> 42:37.505
I suspect Yoyeh.

517
42:37.585 --> 42:39.145
He seems smart.

518
42:40.025 --> 42:43.585
He probably worked with Tangmo to make a plan.

519
42:43.665 --> 42:45.625
He made our team lose today.

520
42:46.825 --> 42:48.505
Cha was a scholarship student too.

521
42:48.585 --> 42:50.225
Aren't you suspicious of him?

522
42:50.825 --> 42:51.945
Are you messing with me?

523
42:52.625 --> 42:54.305
Then he's a scholarship student too.

524
42:54.385 --> 42:55.905
What does Yoyeh have to do with this?

525
42:55.985 --> 42:58.025
Didn't he get a scholarship from your father?

526
42:59.225 --> 43:00.225
He got his money.

527
43:00.905 --> 43:02.585
That counts as a scholarship too.

528
43:02.665 --> 43:05.225
And you got a national team athletic scholarship.

529
43:05.985 --> 43:09.025
If that's the case, we can't rule anyone out.

530
43:13.905 --> 43:16.505
Welcome to the second night's wolf vote.

531
43:17.665 --> 43:18.865
Here he comes again.

532
43:25.825 --> 43:27.145
And now,

533
43:27.905 --> 43:29.745
the results of the second night's vote.

534
43:33.625 --> 43:34.465
Cha.

535
43:37.865 --> 43:39.025
Wut.

536
43:41.745 --> 43:42.825
Wut.

537
43:49.145 --> 43:50.025
Yoyeh.

538
43:55.985 --> 43:56.945
Yoyeh.

539
43:58.425 --> 43:59.265
Cha.

540
44:00.825 --> 44:01.665
Wut.

541
44:03.985 --> 44:04.905
And…

542
44:07.145 --> 44:08.345
Yoyeh.

543
44:13.505 --> 44:15.625
That means tonight,

544
44:17.225 --> 44:19.265
two people are tied in the vote.

545
45:03.025 --> 45:05.745
I'm begging you. Please don't shoot me.

546
45:05.825 --> 45:07.865
My mother is sick and bedridden.

547
45:07.945 --> 45:09.345
Please!

548
45:21.665 --> 45:24.225
Butler, didn't you say the rules…

549
46:12.585 --> 46:15.425
And the person the bodyguard chose to protect tonight

550
46:17.225 --> 46:18.265
is Yoyeh.

551
46:22.225 --> 46:23.505
It's okay.

552
46:23.585 --> 46:25.625
It's okay now. You're safe.

553
46:27.625 --> 46:29.025
Get a hold of yourself.

554
46:29.905 --> 46:31.345
Stay calm.

555
46:31.945 --> 46:33.625
From this moment on,

556
46:34.985 --> 46:36.585
it's time for the wolves

557
46:37.305 --> 46:38.425
to hunt.

558
46:41.225 --> 46:42.585
Good luck, everyone.

559
46:44.985 --> 46:46.705
-He survived. -Hope we all meet again tomorrow morning.

560
46:46.785 --> 46:48.025
Let's go.

561
47:08.825 --> 47:11.945
Yoyeh. Get a hold of yourself.

562
47:17.105 --> 47:19.225
I almost got killed instead of Wut.

563
47:19.825 --> 47:21.665
But you're still here.

564
47:21.745 --> 47:24.465
You're not dead. You're alive.

565
47:25.065 --> 47:26.145
Stay calm.

566
47:41.465 --> 47:42.865
Why are you here?

567
47:46.505 --> 47:49.825
I know you're the bodyguard.

568
47:51.505 --> 47:55.225
The only one who would write Yoyeh's name to protect him is you.

569
47:56.625 --> 47:58.545
Same goes for Capture the Flag.

570
47:59.945 --> 48:01.425
Actually, I knew from day one.

571
48:03.825 --> 48:05.905
What I do is my business.

572
48:06.505 --> 48:07.825
Stay out of it.

573
48:09.425 --> 48:12.345
You really are as stubborn as ever.

574
48:13.225 --> 48:15.345
Have you ever actually played this game?

575
48:15.905 --> 48:18.345
The first person the wolves choose to hunt

576
48:19.705 --> 48:21.185
is the bodyguard.

577
48:21.265 --> 48:23.705
Because once the bodyguard dies,

578
48:27.625 --> 48:29.345
the villagers will have no one to protect them.

579
48:35.505 --> 48:36.985
You'd better watch your backs.

580
48:43.545 --> 48:44.545
Let's go.

581
49:00.225 --> 49:02.345
Surprised? Razor-sharp.

582
49:08.105 --> 49:09.425
You're late.

583
49:10.145 --> 49:11.425
I went to get more weapons.

584
49:13.825 --> 49:16.265
Since you're both here,

585
49:16.865 --> 49:18.025
are either of you

586
49:19.025 --> 49:20.425
a wolf?

587
49:24.465 --> 49:26.665
-No. -No.

588
49:30.225 --> 49:31.745
If I find out if anyone's lying,

589
49:32.305 --> 49:34.025
I'll hunt them down and kill them.

590
49:44.065 --> 49:45.745
You're not scared, are you?

591
49:51.105 --> 49:53.625
There can only be one winner anyway.

592
49:53.705 --> 49:55.625
Wolves or villagers,

593
49:55.705 --> 49:57.545
let's kill them all.

594
50:00.505 --> 50:02.945
How was that? I laughed like a villain.

595
50:04.825 --> 50:06.705
Come on, let's go hunting.

596
50:21.465 --> 50:22.825
-Don't follow me! -Why are you running?

597
50:22.905 --> 50:25.465
-Aren't you tired? Just surrender! -Don't follow me!

598
50:25.545 --> 50:26.745
Leave me alone!

599
50:26.825 --> 50:27.825
Go away!

600
50:30.225 --> 50:32.425
Don't! Help!

601
50:58.425 --> 50:59.625
We need to find somewhere to hide.

602
51:34.625 --> 51:36.145
Please don't hurt me.

603
51:38.505 --> 51:40.305
Let me go.

604
52:59.865 --> 53:01.585
Everything is stated in the contract.

605
53:01.665 --> 53:05.105
Players must follow only the rules of the game.

606
53:05.185 --> 53:06.785
Then what about the people you've killed?

607
53:06.865 --> 53:09.345
-How the fuck is that allowed? -You do realize, don't you?

608
53:09.425 --> 53:11.665
Another death could happen here at any moment.

609
53:11.745 --> 53:13.505
I still want to watch an exciting game

610
53:13.585 --> 53:15.465
played by the rules.

611
53:15.545 --> 53:17.265
I'm sorry I brought you into this game.

612
53:17.345 --> 53:19.025
I'll kill all the wolves,

613
53:19.105 --> 53:21.185
and we'll both survive.

614
53:21.985 --> 53:23.265
I think this reality show

615
53:24.065 --> 53:25.265
is getting weird.

616
53:25.345 --> 53:27.105
If I have to watch someone else kill you,

617
53:27.185 --> 53:29.785
I'd rather be killed by a monstrous ex like you.
